DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("1/((x^2-2*x+3))");
$fun_1 = Formula("((x^4))^(1/2)");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("((4, 5)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (4, 5)) U (4, 5)");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("({-10, -5, -4, 0, 3, 4}) U (-infinity, 15]");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(-infinity, 15] U (-infinity, 15] U ((4, 5))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("((8, infinity) - (8, infinity))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("({-5, 2, 3, 4, 8}) U {-5, 2, 3, 4, 8} U {-5, 2, 3, 4, 8}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

What is the value of [`2*0+17*3`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(51.),width=>5}
---

What is the value of [`15+16+10-15`]? [_____]{answer=>26,width=>10}
---

What is the value of [`10/4+2`]? [_____]{answer=>4.5,width=>6}
---

[`15+15+5+6/1`] is equal to [_____]{Formula('41')}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x > 7\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 1 \leq x \leq 9\}`]
- [`C = \{-5, 2, 3, 4, 8\}`]

Compute:
- [`A - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(C) \cup C \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, -5, -4, 0, 3, 4\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 15\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 4 < x < 5\}`]

Compute:
- [`(C) \cap C \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`(A) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cup B \cup (C) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -9, 10, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 9, -2, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 8, 8, 6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-9, 10, 1>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-9, 10, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-9, 10, 1>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<9, -2, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, 10, 1>") . Compute("<9, -2, 0>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 5, 4, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 5, -5, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -1, 7, -4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, -5, 2>") . Compute("<-1, 7, -4>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<5, -5, 2>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, 7, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-1, 7, -4>") x Compute("<5, -5, 2>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<5, -5, 2>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(4) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>4)}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>5)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
